{"study_accession":"PRJNA727413","secondary_study_accession":"SRP318646","title":"Transcriptome profiles of B cells from MS patients and healthy controls","description":"How epigenetic changes contribute to MS pathogenesis is still poorly understood. Therefore, we conducted a comprehensive analysis of genome-wide DNA methylation patterns in four immune cell populations isolated from MS patients at clinical disease onset. We also performed parallel transcriptome analysis in B cells to better understand the functional consequences of the DNA methylation changes in MS. Overall design: Four immune cell populations, namely CD4+ and CD8+T cells, CD14+ monocytes and CD19+ B cells, were FACS sorted from PBMC samples from a cohort of MS and HC subjects. The total RNA from B cell fractions were used for mRNA-seq.","pubmed":"34911760","geo_series":"","n_samples":37,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN18990209","study_accession":"PRJNA727413","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"MS-8-CD19 RNA-Seq","description":"MS-8-CD19 RNA-Seq","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5278538","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-01-22","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood"],["disease","Multiple sclerosis"],["tissue","peripheral blood"],["cell_type","CD19+ B cells"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR14409208","experiment_accession":"SRX10761347","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"HiSeq X Ten","read_count":37369489,"base_count":11024573919,"first_public":"2022-01-22","experiment_title":"HiSeq X Ten sequencing: GSM5278538: MS-8-CD19 RNA-Seq Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN18990210","study_accession":"PRJNA727413","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"MS-11-CD19 RNA-Seq","description":"MS-11-CD19 RNA-Seq","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5278541","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-01-22","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood"],["disease","Multiple